      "question": "Work out TDCG for Transformer 1 at MAIN at both the first and the last oil sample between 2024-01-15T00:00:00.000000 and 2024-01-19T00:00:00.000000. Add up only hydrogen, methane, ethane, ethylene, acetylene and co, and leave out co2, oxygen and nitrogen. For each of the two samples, give me the timestamp, each gas value and the total. State which IEEE C57.104 condition level each total falls in, using these limits: Condition 1 up to 720 ppm, Condition 2 from 721 to 1920, Condition 3 from 1921 to 4630, and Condition 4 above 4630. Then give the change in TDCG in ppm/day between the two samples. If either sample is missing any of the six gases, don't use it. Move to the next earliest or next latest complete sample, and tell me which timestamps you ended up using.",
      "answer": "Both the first and last oil samples in the window were complete (all six gases present), so no substitution was needed.\n\n**Sample 1 (earliest) \u2014 2024-01-15T00:00:00.000000**\n- Hydrogen: 2845 ppm\n- Methane: 7406 ppm\n- Ethane: 5467 ppm\n- Ethylene: 16684 ppm\n- Acetylene: 7 ppm\n- CO: 32 ppm\n- **TDCG = 32,441 ppm**\n\n**Sample 2 (latest) \u2014 2024-01-18T00:00:00.000000**\n- Hydrogen: 2900 ppm\n- Methane: 7350 ppm\n- Ethane: 5450 ppm\n- Ethylene: 16600 ppm\n- Acetylene: 7 ppm\n- CO: 33 ppm\n- **TDCG = 32,340 ppm**\n\n**IEEE C57.104 condition levels**\n- 2024-01-15: 32,441 ppm \u2192 **Condition 4** (above 4630 ppm)\n- 2024-01-18: 32,340 ppm \u2192 **Condition 4** (above 4630 ppm)\n\n**Change in TDCG**\n- \u0394TDCG = 32,340 \u2212 32,441 = \u2212101 ppm over 3 days\n- **Rate of change \u2248 \u221233.7 ppm/day** (a slight decrease)\n\nTimestamps used: 2024-01-15T00:00:00.000000 and 2024-01-18T00:00:00.000000 (the first and last complete samples in the window \u2014 no missing gases in any sample, so no fallback to other timestamps was required).",
